# Trained model artifacts.
#
# The DEPLOYED set is committed (small, ~2MB total): test_inference.py and
# test_anomaly_detector.py exercise the real pipeline, and model_pipeline.py's
# model *selection* (5-fold CV across RF/GB/MLP/XGBoost) + genetic_optimizer.py's
# feature search are NOT reproducible run-to-run or across sklearn versions --
# so a "regenerate on CI" strategy gives every environment a different model
# and flaky tests. Committing the exact shipped artifacts makes CI and local
# test the same thing. Regenerate deliberately via
# data_prep.py -> genetic_optimizer.py -> model_pipeline.py and review the diff.
*.pkl
!best_model.pkl
!scaler.pkl
!label_encoder.pkl
!anomaly_model.pkl
!anomaly_feature_bounds.json
!feature_info.json
!optimal_features.json

# Derived / report-only, regenerated via data_prep.py / model_pipeline.py:
metrics.json
processed_telemetry.csv

